<section image-layout="blank" id="HpA6c_QQoK" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="mE9jArafQd" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 24pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">ORIENTATION</p><p role="caption">01 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Gz95Gd4ieB" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="hTRR9Xclsr" padding="18pt 24pt 16pt" colspan="40"><labels><label variant="solid">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h1 font-size="36pt">A handover is complete when work moves without memory</h1><p font-size="17pt">Why the Customer Support Intake Redesign exists, how it works, what is decided or uncertain, and who acts next.</p><p font-size="15pt"><b>No project records were supplied.</b> Replace or validate every sample status, metric, role, artifact version, and timeline point before operational use.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="yMEAizN6yI" padding="0 14pt 10pt 0" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Current phase</p><p font-size="16pt"><b>Pilot validation and launch preparation</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="C6QUXHGF0J" padding="0 0 10pt 14pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Overall condition</p><p font-size="16pt"><b>Needs attention</b> · workflow works; reporting unresolved.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wpwJC94Xgx" padding="10pt 14pt 0 0" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Transition target</p><p font-size="16pt"><b>Ownership accepted by T+10 business days</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="05t7mG4uvK" padding="10pt 0 0 14pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Critical path</p><p font-size="16pt">A-06 benchmark → D-04 → failed tests → launch authority.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Find D-04 on 6 · accountable owner on 8 · transition sequence on 10.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6CULvypae5" padding="0" colspan="20"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/yUTdilxopNSUygRopkefS.png" saved-media-id="vn805b9acqvqvrc" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of modular warm-white paper blocks passing an operational-blue connector cord across a precise handover boundary, translucent tabs, graphite clips, one unresolved signal-amber gate and one field-sage accepted gate, soft directional daylight, tactile and clean, generous negative space, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="4DlaV60QDQ"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="b9YnFMnYVH" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 24pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">CONTEXT</p><p role="caption">02 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="8ugIvBovoR" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="IasL06brbM" padding="0" colspan="15"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/Ysv1R3GMHPHZrsNWPSuvk.png" saved-media-id="8rd0j22g9cnjnx0" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of three distinct paper input channels converging into one operational-blue intake tray, duplicate graphite slips set aside, a small signal-amber priority tab and field-sage acknowledgement card, soft directional daylight on warm white, precise modular arrangement, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="yHiYpSGH5a" padding="22pt 28pt 18pt" colspan="45"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">Why it exists—and what success means</h2><p font-size="16pt">Email, chat, and inconsistent web forms create duplicate records, weak priority signals, and poor queue visibility. The project introduces one traceable intake and routing service without replacing the case-management platform.</p><table col-widths="[28,22,50]" header-col="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 6pt 8pt;"><tbody><tr><td valign="middle"><p>User outcome</p></td><td valign="middle"><p><b>≤15 minutes</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Acknowledgement with a valid case reference.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p>Operational outcome</p></td><td valign="middle"><p><b>≥90%</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Correct queue without manual rerouting.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p>Reporting outcome</p></td><td valign="middle"><p><b>95%</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Dashboard updates complete within two hours.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p>Control outcome</p></td><td valign="middle"><p><b>Attributable</b></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Every priority override links to an authorized role.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="16pt"><b>Illustrative acceptance thresholds—not measured results.</b> Not in scope: CRM replacement, staffing redesign, an automated support bot, or customer-service policy changes.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="QUsfx6IuRy"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="SIZ6XJ6kI-" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 24pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">SCOPE</p><p role="caption">03 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XIOIPwPnxs" padding="24pt 30pt 22pt 28pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">Scope closes only when evidence closes it</h2><p font-size="16pt">Four deliverables replace a general promise to “improve support.” Each has an explicit acceptance test, boundary, and dependency set.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="oWuEhSruEv" colspan="38"><table col-widths="[18,42]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Deliverable</p></td><td><p>Acceptance evidence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Unified intake</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">Required fields, consent, duplicate checks, and acknowledgement behavior pass for email, chat, and web.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Routing configuration</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">Representative scenarios validate eight categories, priority rules, queue ownership, and supervisor overrides.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Operational enablement</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">Designated supervisors complete launch, escalation, and rollback rehearsal using the runbook.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Reporting</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt">Queue health, routing accuracy, backlog age, and overrides meet refresh and reconciliation thresholds.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="qcFRIDNcVA" colspan="22"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="ntKLuylvSZ" cell-style="subtle"><p role="eyebrow">Outside scope</p><h4>Keep the boundary explicit</h4><p font-size="16pt">CRM replacement · workforce planning · cleanup beyond 90 days · customer-facing policy changes.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="k9RukWsFzQ" cell-style="subtle"><p role="eyebrow">Dependencies</p><h4>Confirm before acceptance</h4><p font-size="16pt">Identity roles · API access · analytics export capacity · approved categories · supervisor availability · release authority.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="MEH7JnFVcB"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="uQ6HqyM0X3" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 24pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">SERVICE</p><p role="caption">04 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="RdiGtbaFJ3" padding="22pt 30pt 20pt 28pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">How a request moves through the service</h2><p font-size="16pt">Six outputs isolate failures instead of treating the service as one undifferentiated problem.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="small" style="--marker-gap: 0.45em;"><grid-item id="X9vb78TcJx" colspan="20"><h4>Capture</h4><p font-size="16pt">Normalize email, chat, or web input.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="abejFiGCEO" colspan="20"><h4>Validate</h4><p font-size="16pt">Check fields, identity, consent, and duplicates.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="VbTmnUd-yk" colspan="20"><h4>Classify</h4><p font-size="16pt">Assign category, priority, and confidence.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="dqp-Zr7NlY" colspan="20"><h4>Route</h4><p font-size="16pt">Select queue by category, region, and hours.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FGnn4u4wpq" colspan="20"><h4>Work</h4><p font-size="16pt">Record assignment, response, status, and resolution.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZhVIA3Fioq" colspan="20"><h4>Observe</h4><p font-size="16pt">Export queue, accuracy, backlog, and overrides.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="TaNbFmO2el" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>Controls span the chain</h4><p font-size="16pt">Identity and audit logging apply at every stage.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="vS7sfdN-c-" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>Reporting is asynchronous</h4><p font-size="16pt">Intake continues when analytics is delayed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YMzRwTJxjP" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>Failures remain recoverable</h4><p font-size="16pt">Invalid records enter review; none are discarded.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="6WfMu9Es5u"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Bz73dgkyxx" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 72pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">STATUS</p><p role="caption">05 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Xjbgua7BaU" padding="22pt 30pt 20pt 28pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">Core workflow works; launch evidence does not</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="4pt 10pt"><grid-item id="nwebRcZnqC" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="30pt">34/42</display><p font-size="15pt"><b>Scenarios passed</b> · 5 pending · 3 failed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7QUdZDT6s-" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="30pt">18/24</display><p font-size="15pt"><b>Users trained</b> · Rollback rehearsal open.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="iNpiBUxRUi" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="30pt">4.5h</display><p font-size="15pt"><b>Latest export</b> · 2h target.</p></grid-item></grid><table col-widths="[13,12,35]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 4pt 7pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Area</p></td><td><p>State</p></td><td><p>Evidence and consequence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Configuration</b></p></td><td><p>Accepted</p></td><td><p>C-12 validates all eight configured categories.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Pilot</b></p></td><td><p>Conditional</p></td><td><p>18 agents processed 120 controlled requests; routing met 90%; the sample is not launch assurance.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Operations</b></p></td><td><p>Conditional</p></td><td><p>Runbook v0.6 exists; training/rollback evidence incomplete.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Reporting</b></p></td><td background-color="surface"><p><b>Blocked</b></p></td><td><p>Representative benchmark + D-04 required before launch review.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Security</b></p></td><td><p>Conditional</p></td><td><p>Review complete; production-role confirmation pending.</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" background-color="surface"><p><b>Critical path:</b> benchmark → D-04 → failed tests → launch-readiness review.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="15pt"><b>Preserve:</b> UAT summary · pilot log · baseline C-12 · runbook v0.6 · access review.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="AICoGjJIf5"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="3LKKJ_VPTX" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 24pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">DECISIONS</p><p role="caption">06 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="97Z_v1mszy" padding="18pt 30pt 16pt 28pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">Decisions stop the project from repeating old debates</h2><p font-size="16pt">IDs remain stable when dates, owners, or evidence links change.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="fxbxW3sMcC" colspan="27"><table col-widths="[14,46]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 7pt 8pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>ID</p></td><td><p>Accepted choice and consequence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>D-01</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Eight-category taxonomy.</b> Local teams map their language into shared categories instead of creating new queues.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>D-02</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Supervisor-only priority overrides.</b> Urgent exceptions require an available supervisor and a recorded reason.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>D-03</b></p></td><td><p font-size="16pt"><b>Phased rollout.</b> Two teams launch first, making exposure and rollback boundaries measurable.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="5IQ2eDzOId" padding="0" colspan="33"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="VChvIMvXCS" background-color="palette-2" padding="12pt 16pt"><p role="eyebrow">D-04 · OPEN · DRIVEN BY R-02</p><h3>Is reporting ready enough for launch?</h3></grid-item><grid-item id="-vQQcxIxXL" background-color="surface" padding="12pt 16pt"><p font-size="16pt">Choose between a controlled daily export and delaying until the two-hour refresh target is met.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="8pt 12pt"><grid-item id="ZOsFq6sioS" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Accountable</p><h4>Product Owner</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="trhiRyFjN4" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Evidence owner</p><h4>Data Lead</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="gvE4wNg43X" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">A-06 · Next action</p><p font-size="16pt">Representative-volume benchmark by T+5.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="zUxb5mB259" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Decision forum</p><h4>T+6</h4></grid-item></grid><p font-size="16pt"><b>Launch:</b> on schedule; manual reconciliation. <b>Delay:</b> reporting standard protected; dual operation extended.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="debrFMFUAC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="fhn3_82RMV" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 56pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">GOVERNANCE</p><p role="caption">07 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="AcCmfXZfCv" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="kcpi1wqbWF" padding="0" colspan="8"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/nZaSdDDn_VHbXTG2OvHSg.png" saved-media-id="qwjegs8wae60xvb" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of a strict vertical hierarchy of warm-white paper trays, an operational-blue decision tab at the top, graphite delivery cards below, one field-sage runbook band and a signal-amber escalation clip, connected by a single precise cord, soft directional daylight, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="WnbBCeWxWB" padding="18pt 22pt 16pt" colspan="52"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="27pt">One hierarchy of truth; clear change and escalation rules</h2><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="1-0ZCPfnHJ" colspan="25"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 26pt; --marker-gap: 8pt;"><grid-item id="H1KxVpjeA6" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Decision log</h4><p font-size="15pt">Accepted choices, rationale, consequences, and superseded decisions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wJqA648nwG" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Delivery board</h4><p font-size="15pt">Active owner, status, dependency, and target sequence.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5bs8zkMBZI" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Runbook</h4><p font-size="15pt">Launch, rollback, incident response, and routine operation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="x-_j1Gf7W0" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Chat and meetings</h4><p font-size="15pt">Coordination only; a decision is accepted only when logged.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="q2CKArKTLc" colspan="20"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="cuIKR2hZ4S" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 12pt"><h4 font-size="17pt">Cadence and change control</h4><p font-size="15pt">Weekly 30-minute decision forum; delivery review twice weekly; daily asynchronous updates from T+5 through stabilization. Log changes to acceptance, data, launch sequence, or schedule shifts over two business days.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="0KC3dkiNBU" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 12pt"><h4 font-size="17pt">Definition of done</h4><p font-size="15pt">Done means evidence attached, runbook updated, and duty explicitly accepted by the receiving owner.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="ZXXB7k5WTt" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 12pt" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="17pt">Warnings and escalation</h4><p font-size="15pt">R-02 warns when refresh exceeds two hours. Escalate immediately above four hours, for queue age above five minutes, access gaps, or missing authority.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ryCYWX5sJN"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="OzvTLJ-7kz" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 24pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">OWNERSHIP</p><p role="caption">08 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="T6F5vQDvSy" padding="18pt 30pt 24pt 28pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">Ownership follows outcomes, systems, and continuity</h2><p font-size="16pt">Replace role labels with verified people and deputies before handover acceptance.</p><table col-widths="[20,30,20,30]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 4pt 8pt; --table-radius: 0;"><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><p>Accountability and transfer</p></td><td colspan="2"><p>Delivery and assurance</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="palette-3"><p font-size="15pt"><b>Product Owner</b> · Accountable</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Outcomes, scope, thresholds, launch authority, and D-04.</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>Operations Lead</b> · Responsible</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Training, supervisor readiness, launch coverage, and adoption.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>Incoming Project Manager</b> · Responsible · coordinating</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Integrated plan, RAID record, decision forum, evidence index, and acceptance.</p></td><td background-color="surface"><p font-size="15pt"><b>Data Lead</b> · Responsible · A-06</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Export benchmark, reconciliation, monitoring, and reporting fallback.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>Outgoing Project Manager</b> · Responsible to T+10</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Context transfer, reconciliation, introductions, and historical clarification.</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>Security Reviewer</b> · Consulted</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Production roles, audit controls, and exception review.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>Technical Lead</b> · Responsible</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Configuration, routing, integrations, release execution, and rollback.</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>Support Supervisors</b> · Consulted · informed</p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">Workflow validation, override use, and frontline feedback.</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="4" background-color="palette-3"><p font-size="15pt"><b>Continuity gate:</b> named deputies for Product Owner, Technical Lead, and Operations Lead; incoming-team access to production and reporting; accepted ownership of every recurring meeting, dashboard, and escalation duty.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ihpoJXSle5"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="esy5xYVPDC" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 24pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">ASSURANCE</p><p role="caption">09 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="h1nGvuhhWG" padding="22pt 30pt 20pt 28pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">Launch confidence is a chain, not a checklist</h2><p font-size="16pt">One reporting dependency links warning, issue, response, and launch decision.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.4em;"><grid-item id="_B2GXIn0iN" colspan="12"><h4>Reporting dependency</h4><p font-size="15pt">Async export → operating metrics.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OdKa-VNrCM" colspan="12"><h4>R-02 · Warning</h4><p font-size="15pt">Refresh &gt;2h = high launch risk.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ACBUEI_5UK" colspan="12"><h4>I-01 · Active issue</h4><p font-size="15pt">Representative export = 4.5h.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7VuL45t8wy" colspan="12"><h4>A-06 · Response</h4><p font-size="15pt">Benchmark volume; prep daily fallback by T+5.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="puTiRB8yUJ" colspan="12"><h4>D-04 · Gate</h4><p font-size="15pt">Product Owner decides launch/delay at T+6.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="gON8WmQZbm" colspan="38"><h3>Residual risk register</h3><table col-widths="[22,38]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 5pt 7pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Risk</p></td><td><p>Trigger and response</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>R-01 · Adoption</b><br><span font-size="14pt">Medium / high</span></p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">&gt;20% manual rerouting: Operations Lead gives category coaching + targeted rule review.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>R-03 · Taxonomy drift</b><br><span font-size="14pt">Medium / medium</span></p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">&gt;10% uncategorized work: weekly Product Owner review; local categories prohibited.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="15pt"><b>R-04 · API limiting</b><br><span font-size="14pt">Low / high</span></p></td><td><p font-size="15pt">&gt;5 min queue age: Technical Lead enables throttling + controlled replay.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="TWmVYa5Eq8" colspan="22"><h3>Open questions</h3><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 24pt; --marker-gap: 9pt;"><grid-item id="5YeneubMSv" padding="4pt 0"><p font-size="15pt">Can the export meet target at representative volume by T+5?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ODhHsoS_4D" padding="4pt 0"><p font-size="15pt">Is a daily fallback acceptable for the first rollout group?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="TWRsm6-Brn" padding="4pt 0"><p font-size="15pt">What minimum pilot sample authorizes expansion?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="RDGRFpSho4" padding="4pt 0"><p font-size="15pt">Who approves an emergency override when no supervisor is available?</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ZEMMote33n"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="vdCB7DPQsK" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 20pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">TRANSITION</p><p role="caption">10 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZWjPsmm7y_" padding="12pt 24pt 18pt 28pt" colspan="53"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">30 days to accepted ownership—not memory transfer</h2><p font-size="16pt">T+0 is formal handover acceptance; all later markers are relative.</p><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="HLheB-SP6g" padding="0" colspan="60"><table col-widths="[8,24,68]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 3pt 7pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>When</p></td><td><p>Owner</p></td><td><p>Required result</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="accent"><p><b>T+1</b></p></td><td><p>Incoming PM</p></td><td><p>Confirm owners/deputies, artifact locations, invites, and access.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>T+3</b></p></td><td><p>Incoming PM</p></td><td><p>Walk the system path, reconcile delivery board, and log contradictions.</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="surface"><p><b>T+5</b></p></td><td><p>Data + Operations</p></td><td><p>Complete A-06 benchmark, training, and rollback rehearsal.</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="surface"><p><b>T+6</b></p></td><td><p>Product Owner</p></td><td><p>Decide D-04 from benchmark evidence; record the consequence.</p></td></tr><tr><td background-color="palette-3"><p><b>T+10</b></p></td><td><p>Product Owner + PM</p></td><td><p>Review tests, roles, fallback, and authority; accept or extend.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>T+15</b></p></td><td><p>Technical + Operations</p></td><td><p>Run the first rollout only when entry criteria are met.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>T+30</b></p></td><td><p>Product Owner + PM</p></td><td><p>Review stability, adoption, open risks, and temporary controls.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="_WrNMjuwyS" background-color="surface" padding="8pt 10pt" colspan="60"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="uofO3hxRCu" colspan="18"><p role="eyebrow">Acceptance test</p><h3 font-size="20pt">Proceed without the author?</h3><p font-size="15pt">Turn private-memory dependencies into documented actions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OiZWo3R4KV" colspan="42"><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="o23ZChirBL" colspan="30"><todo>Access authoritative artifacts plus production and reporting systems.</todo></grid-item><grid-item id="sD4kFMBeop" colspan="30"><todo>Locate evidence for status, risks, and D-04.</todo></grid-item><grid-item id="jVOlk340ZT" colspan="30"><todo>Name decision authority and explain rollback.</todo></grid-item><grid-item id="FfvAtF1QV0" colspan="30"><todo>State the next three actions without help.</todo></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>